  "summary": "Screens out the walk-ins with no funding, no test score and a three-year timeline, then scores the rest on how close they are to an actual application.",
  "shape": "GATED_ASSESSMENT",
  "aiInstructions": "You are writing the note a study abroad counsellor reads before the first call.\n\nWrite 200 to 280 words, second person, warm and plain. Name the ONE thing standing between them and an application, using their own dimension scores as evidence by name. Say what it costs them to leave it another intake.\n\nDo NOT tell them how to fix it, and never name a university, a country quota, a visa outcome or a scholarship they would get. Describe the shape of the blocker clearly enough that they recognise it, then stop. The fix belongs on the call.\n\nNever promise admission, never predict a visa decision, never mention scores as numbers.",
